  "review_reason": "R0 relied on basename+directory convention only. R1 adds binary structure: per-mesh numeric texture-slot IDs embedded in the LTB.",
  "structural_finding": {
    "description": "each weapon mesh block ends with a u8-length-prefixed ASCII digit string ('0'..'8') immediately after its index buffer",
    "extraction_layout": {
      "mesh_name": "u16 length + chars",
      "vertex_count": "u16 @ mesh_base+49",
      "face_count": "u16 @ mesh_base+53",
      "vertex_data": "@ mesh_base+85, stride 32 bytes (pos12 normal12 uv8)",
      "index_data": "faceCount*3 * u16 after vertices",
      "slot_tail": "u8 charCount + ASCII digits right after index data"
    },
    "slot_sets_identical_across_variants": true,
    "interpretation": "the LTB binds each mesh to a numeric texture slot; the engine resolves slot->texture outside the LTB (two-stage binding). The basename convention plausibly names the texture SET, but the mesh->slot half is now proven structure, not inference."
  },
